# What is served from whatholdsup.org, and what is not.
#
# Until 2026-08-27 everything in this directory was deployed, so
# https://whatholdsup.org/email/send_broadcast.py returned 200 and served our
# sending logic, and the gate reports were fetchable alongside it. Neither was
# a decision. Nothing secret was exposed — credentials are environment
# variables — but a directory is not an access policy.

# Operational tooling. Not part of the publication.
email/
*.py
__pycache__/

# Gate reports. Publishing these may well be a good idea — they are the full
# record of every objection raised against a draft, including the ones we
# rejected and why, which is the most honest thing we could put on the site.
# But it should be a decision with a page built for it, not a JSON file
# sitting at a guessable URL. Excluded until that decision is made.
*.gate.json

# Editor and tooling leftovers. cmd_publish does `git add site/whatholdsup`,
# so anything that lands in this directory is committed and served unless it
# is named here. A .bak of the assessment sat here for four minutes on
# 2026-08-28 and would have been deployed beside it.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
.DS_Store
